# A COLOSSUS'S FOOT IN THE REGION (slice 3: 19_colossi, colossus_foot.gd, the
# craters gen_treads.gd cut). The straddling walker is staged twenty world
# minutes after its foot came down in this world's first tread. Under the ankle
# first -- a drum three hundred metres across standing its own height over the
# player, its vents and its ring of cold light the ceiling, the three toes
# arching down to their pads -- over the shoulder and looking up, then top-down.
# Then outside a crater, facing its pad: the forty-metre disc on the bared floor,
# the strata stepped up round it, the spoil on the lip; and top-down there.
# Run it at noon and at night (the ring under the drum lights the ground between
# the toes). Not with `hour`: the walk IS the clock, and ten hours on the foot
# has lifted and gone. The run opens over the shoulder; `hold shoulder` is the
# top-down view; the glide back down to the shoulder takes its own bearing, so
# the tour lets it land before standing anywhere that says which way to face.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_tread.tour --seed=7 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0+20 --hour=12 --view=shoulder --weather=clear:0
#   tools/tour.sh tours/colossi_tread.tour --seed=7 --place=tread0 --colossus=2@tread0+20 --hour=22.5 --view=shoulder --weather=clear:0
await colossus_foot 30
await colossus_tread 5
near colossus_foot
mouse 0,-120 0.3
wait 2
shot 00-under-the-ankle
mouse 0,-1400 1
wait 1
shot 01-looking-up-at-the-drum
hold shoulder
wait 1.5
shot 02-top-down-under-the-ankle
release shoulder
wait 1
near colossus_pad
wait 2
shot 03-at-a-crater-facing-its-pad
hold shoulder
wait 1.5
shot 04-top-down-at-a-crater
release shoulder
